────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Iteration 2 declared tier 2: single mechanism + multi-knob OR ablation OR dose-response on one knob
  Justification: iter 2 — single mechanism (P/D disaggregation latency) + dose-response on arrival rate
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  SUMMARY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  We are testing whether BLIS faithfully reproduces the paper's predictions about prefill/decode disaggregation latency: specifically that Always-Disaggregate (AD) yields lower inter-token latency (ITL) but higher time-to-first-token (TTFT) than Always-Local (AL), and that ITL increases monotonically with arrival rate following the 1/(1−ρ) utilization model. This is iteration 2 of the pd-latency-model-validation family, a tier-2 single-mechanism dose-response design.

  * 54 total runs: 9 arrival rates (5–150 req/s) × 2 modes (AL via pd-decider=never, AD via pd-decider=always) × 3 seeds (42,43,44). Each run sends 300 requests with fixed 512 prompt / 128 output tokens to a 4-instance cluster (2 prefill + 2 decode) using the trained-physics latency model.
  * h-main (core claim): ITL_AD < ITL_AL and TTFT_AD > TTFT_AL at every rate-seed pair. Confirmation requires all 27 ITL gaps (AL−AD) positive and all 27 TTFT gaps (AD−AL) positive. A single consistent sign violation at any rate-seed refutes the directional prediction.
  * h-dose-response: mean ITL must increase monotonically with rate for both AL and AD, validating the 1/(1−ρ) queuing model. A non-monotonic reversal (ITL dropping as rate increases) would indicate batch-size capping, preemption artifacts, or failure to reach steady state at high rates.
  * h-tradeoff: AD's TTFT penalty over AL should stay ≤15 ms, bounded by the fixed KV transfer cost (~3.4 ms) plus modest prefill-pool queueing. Exceeding 15 ms would suggest prefill-pool saturation at high rates, requiring re-examination of the prefill utilization assumptions.
  * Key defaults left unlocked are safe: KV blocks=1M (no eviction risk at 300×640 tokens), max_model_len=unlimited, FCFS scheduler, pd_transfer_contention=off. Each run completes in <3s wall time, so total experiment wall time is ~3 minutes.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

